# The fusions that owe an exact composed remainder. One row per composed layer whose demand and
# nameplate eliminations are both answered, so the remainder worked out from its parts is a figure
# rather than a warning.
#
# A difference whose left operand is a file
#   A difference whose left side is spelt out inline cannot be counted, so no law on
#   algebra/roster.sqlc could govern it. `composition/fusions.sqlc` is the left side,
#   `composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc` the right, and algebra/owed_remainder.sqlc counts them.
#   composition/carriable.sqlc exists for the same reason at the other difference.
#
# The remainder's counterpart of the sums
#   composition/owed_equality.sqlc owes a sum per quantity. A remainder needs both the demand and
#   the nameplate answered, so the two populations differ, and neither stands in for the other.
#
# It makes `coalesce(e, 0)` right one join later
#   Once the suspended fusions are out, an absent elimination means the composer looked and found no
#   double counting, which is the number zero. Inside the suspended set the same blank means nobody
#   looked, and filling it would put a claim in the check that the document declined to make.
-- composition/fusions.sqlc less composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc.
SELECT f.filing, f.layer
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/fusions.sqlc)
) f
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(composition/suspended_remainders.sqlc)
) s ON s.composition = f.filing AND s.composed_layer = f.layer
WHERE s.composition IS NULL
